celeste-linux (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * About section in Settings: version, project page and releases links,
    GPL-3.0-only licence notice, no telemetry.
  * App icon unified with the Android build: same green-and-white launcher
    icon on the window, taskbar and menu entry.
  * MCP tool servers: per-server enable/disable, trust approval gate with
    “always allow”, audit log, HTTP-only on Android.
  * Per-persona long-term memory with add/forget/clear notes.
  * Backup export can exclude credentials: passwords and API keys, MCP
    environment values and headers, URL userinfo and query strings, and
    credential flag values are redacted after an explicit plain-text
    confirmation. A redacted export keeps every other field, including
    persona chats, artwork, message images and schedules.
  * Importing a backup restores MCP servers disabled with trust ASK and never
    restores trusted certificate pins.
  * The pinned TLS trust manager fails closed on a null or empty certificate
    chain instead of treating it as trusted.
  * Version bumped to 0.2.2.

 -- Nikos <nikos@localhost>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:45:00 +0300

celeste-linux (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug-fix update from two adversarial reviews: the filesystem gate now
    refuses hard-linked files; spontaneous deliveries keep their re-armed
    successor; settings recovery never logs the file's contents; all
    helper-process reads are deadline-bounded; MCP transports survive a
    wedged server or a timed-out request and rethrow cancellation; approval
    timeouts are reported accurately; shared payloads land visibly; persona
    names cannot inject .desktop keys; same-session float settings read back
    correctly.
  * Version bumped to 0.2.0.

 -- Nikos <nikos@localhost>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:40:14 +0300

celeste-linux (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: the jpackage app image with its own trimmed runtime under
    /usr/lib/celeste-linux, the application menu entry, the hicolor icon and the
    systemd user unit (installed, not enabled). The ONNX Runtime jar is cut to
    the platform this package can load, 90 MB -> 5.7 MB, and the build refuses
    to proceed if the cut has nothing to cut (PLAN.md §4, §10/M6).

 -- Nikos <nikos@localhost>  Thu, 16 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0300
